// The Eastern Interconnection: the United States east of the Rockies and the
// Canadian provinces synchronised with it (Saskatchewan, Manitoba, Ontario,
// New Brunswick, Nova Scotia and Prince Edward Island). Quebec and ERCOT run
// their own interconnections and are cut out. The Texas Panhandle stays in:
// it is synchronised with the Eastern grid through SPS.
//
// Geography is at diorama fidelity: polygons follow the real coastlines and
// interconnection seams closely enough to read on a 100 x 60 grid (about
// 0.5 degrees per cell), and a few shores are nudged so that lakeside metros
// sit on land. Points are (lon, lat) in degrees.
//
// Seam with the Western Interconnection (shared with
// western_interconnection.ron): the Alberta-Saskatchewan line (110 W) to the
// 49th parallel, the Montana-Dakota line (104.05 W) to the Nebraska-Colorado
// line, the Colorado border, then south through eastern New Mexico along
// 104.5 W to the Rio Grande.
//
// The two files trace this seam with the same vertices, so the polygons agree
// exactly. The grids do not (this one is 0.51 x 0.525 degrees, the Western one
// 0.39 x 0.40), and a cell is playable when its centre is, so three pairs of
// cells straddled the seam: each Eastern centre fell in a Western land cell
// and each Western centre in an Eastern one. Two pairs sit on the Colorado
// border (Eastern cells (14, 36) and (15, 36), centred at 36.8375 N in the
// Oklahoma Panhandle, against Western cells (58, 57) and (59, 57), whose
// centres lie on the 37 N border itself). The Panhandle is Eastern (SPS), so
// those two are cut from the Western file, not this one. The third pair is
// Eastern cell (12, 39) against Western cell (55, 61) in eastern New Mexico,
// where both centres are true to their side of the diagonal seam; the
// coarser grid gives way, so the last `exclude` ring here removes cell
// (12, 39). With the three cuts no centre is playable in both regions.
(
    region_schema: 4,
    id: "eastern_interconnection",
    system_zone: 1,
    time_zones: [
        (id: 1, name_key: "zone-et", standard_offset_minutes: -300, dst_months: [false, false, true, true, true, true, true, true, true, true, false, false]),
